iMac 18,3 CS8409/CS42L83: follow the jack for capture, so the mic switches with the headset.

Applies to the snd_hda_macbookpro DKMS driver (davidjo/snd_hda_macbookpro),
against the tree at commit be90113. Confirmed on hardware.

Output already followed the jack -- plug a headset in and playback moves to
the headphones, unplug and it returns to the speakers. Capture did not.
With a headset plugged in, recording was completely silent: peak amplitude
exactly 0.00000, while the stream itself ran and reported no error.

The driver already knows how to set up both microphones. On plugin,
cs_8409_pcm_capture_pre_prepare_hook calls cs_8409_headcapture_setup, which
routes the headset mike (pin 0x3c) to the CS42L83 ADC 0x1a; with nothing
plugged in it calls cs_8409_capture_setup, which brings up the internal mike
on intmike_adc_nid (0x23 on the iMacs, 0x22 on the MacBook Pros). What it
never did was move the capture PCM. hinfo->nid stays on intmike_adc_nid
forever, so with a headset in, the driver configured the headset mike and
then recorded from the internal mike's converter -- which nothing had
switched on. Hence silence rather than the wrong microphone.

Two things follow from that. cs_8409_store_stream_format caches the DMA
stream tag against hinfo->nid, so the nid has to be corrected BEFORE the pre
prepare hook runs, otherwise cs_8409_really_update_stream_format(0x1a, ...)
inside the headset setup finds an empty cache. And the switch has to work in
both directions: hinfo is persistent for the life of the codec, so switching
only on plugin would strand the PCM on 0x1a and break the internal mike for
every recording after the headset was unplugged once.

So: in cs_8409_capture_pcm_prepare, pick the ADC that the hook is about to
configure -- 0x1a when a mike-equipped headset is present, intmike_adc_nid
otherwise -- and if it differs from the current one, cleanup the old stream
and repoint hinfo->nid. The guard only ever moves between those two nids, so
any other capture nid is left alone.

The second hunk covers a headset that presents no mike (a 3 pole plug). That
case fell through a "I think this is impossible" comment and set nothing up
at all, which was the other way to get a silent capture while plugged in.
Fall back to the internal mike there.

Provenance: the ADC switch is the idea behind ExternPointer's
davidjo/snd_hda_macbookpro PR #197 (open, unmerged), which switches
hinfo->nid to 0x1a when jack_present && have_mike. That PR only switches one
way, so once the headset came out the PCM stayed on 0x1a; the version here is
bidirectional, which is what makes unplug work. The rest of PR #197 is not
taken: its Makefile hunk turns on the MYSOUNDDEBUG build, its dkms.conf hunk
is already in this tree, its second capture_pcm_prepare hunk edits
patch_cirrus_apple.h (the pre-6.17 build variant -- this kernel builds
cirrus_apple.h), and its capture gain change (0x27 -> 0x33) is unrelated to
routing. Its cs_8409_linein_volume_setup fix, writing newgain instead of a
hardcoded 0x000060a7, is a real bug but computes the same value at the
volume actually used, so it is left out to keep this patch to one subject.

ExternPointer's other patch from issue #29, which makes cs_8409_capture_setup
run unconditionally, is deliberately NOT applied. It forces the internal mike
on even with a headset plugged in, which is the opposite of switching, and it
removes cs_8409_intmike_linein_resetup() from the unplug path -- the call
that brings the internal mike back when the headset comes out.

Verified on iMac18,3, kernel 7.1.9-arch1-2, codec subsystem id 0x106b1000,
with a mike-equipped headset in the 3.5mm jack: capture DMA lands on ADC
0x1a (Converter: stream=1), pin 0x3c reads Pin-ctls: 0x20: IN and the
internal mike pin 0x45 reads 0x00, and recording gives peak 0.0253 where it
was 0.00000. Output still moves to the headphones and back, the hardware
alsa_output.pci-0000_00_1f.3.analog-stereo sink is unaffected, and repeated
back-to-back captures work.

diff --git a/patch_cirrus/cirrus_apple.h b/patch_cirrus/cirrus_apple.h
index 7e9bcd1..a7d0f7f 100644
--- a/patch_cirrus/cirrus_apple.h
+++ b/patch_cirrus/cirrus_apple.h
@@ -792,6 +792,38 @@ static int cs_8409_capture_pcm_prepare(struct hda_pcm_stream *hinfo,
         mycodec_info(codec, "cs_8409_capture_pcm_prepare: NID=0x%x, stream=0x%x, format=0x%x\n",
                   hinfo->nid, stream_tag, format);
 
+	// Follow the jack: point the capture PCM at whichever ADC is actually going
+	// to be set up by the pre prepare hook below.
+	//   headset with a mike plugged in -> cs_8409_headcapture_setup routes the
+	//     headset mike (pin 0x3c) to the cs42l83 ADC 0x1a
+	//   nothing plugged in (or a 3 pole headset with no mike)
+	//     -> cs_8409_capture_setup brings up the internal mike on intmike_adc_nid
+	// This has to happen BEFORE the hook so that cs_8409_store_stream_format
+	// caches the DMA stream tag against the right nid - otherwise
+	// cs_8409_really_update_stream_format(0x1a,...) inside the headset setup
+	// finds an empty cache and we get a stream bound to one ADC while the other
+	// one is the one that was configured, ie silence.
+	// NOTE both directions are needed - hinfo is persistent for the life of the
+	// codec, so switching only on plugin would strand the PCM on 0x1a for every
+	// later recording once the headset had been unplugged.
+	{
+		hda_nid_t want_nid;
+
+		if (spec->jack_present && spec->have_mike)
+			want_nid = 0x1a;
+		else
+			want_nid = spec->intmike_adc_nid;
+
+		if (hinfo->nid != want_nid &&
+		    (hinfo->nid == 0x1a || hinfo->nid == spec->intmike_adc_nid))
+		{
+			dev_info(hda_codec_dev(codec),
+			         "cs_8409_capture_pcm_prepare: capture nid 0x%02x -> 0x%02x (jack %d mike %d)\n",
+			         hinfo->nid, want_nid, spec->jack_present, spec->have_mike);
+			snd_hda_codec_cleanup_stream(codec, hinfo->nid);
+			hinfo->nid = want_nid;
+		}
+	}
 
         cs_8409_pcm_capture_pre_prepare_hook(hinfo, codec, stream_tag, format, substream,
                               HDA_GEN_PCM_ACT_PREPARE);
diff --git a/patch_cirrus/patch_cirrus_new84.h b/patch_cirrus/patch_cirrus_new84.h
index a40a6f5..a974f43 100644
--- a/patch_cirrus/patch_cirrus_new84.h
+++ b/patch_cirrus/patch_cirrus_new84.h
@@ -1804,8 +1804,12 @@ static void cs_8409_pcm_capture_pre_prepare_hook(struct hda_pcm_stream *hinfo, s
 						spec->headset_capture_format_setup_needed = 0;
 					}
 				}
-				// I think this is impossible - this would say we tried to capture
-				// using a headset without mike
+				else
+				{
+					// headset/headphones with no mike (3 pole plug) - fall back to
+					// the internal mike so capture still works while plugged in
+					cs_8409_capture_setup(codec);
+				}
 				// NOTE - still not fixed linein/lineout working - this may need
 				// changing here
 			}
